          "en": "False. The passage refers to a masquerade as \"a ritual ceremony performed before a community. Some masquerades are entertainment – a parade, for example, or dance that reinforces the cultural identity of a community...the masquerader may serve as a kind of moral policeman: instructing, punishing, maintaining and restoring order, or presiding over a passage...\"",
